es="100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="hero-inner wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Fountain of Hope</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href="/#topics">Topics</a><span class="sep">/</span><span class="here">Topic 03</span></nav><div class="hero-kicker"><span style="color:#FF9CBE;font-weight:700">WASH · COMMUNITY RESILIENCE</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Garissa County</span></div><h1>Clean water, and the <em>dignity it brings.</em></h1><p class="hero-sub">In one of Kenya’s driest counties, water decides everything — a mother’s safety, a child’s health, a community’s future. Fountain of Hope works for clean, safe water, and the resilience that comes with it.</p><div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="#story">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M19 12l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#topics">All topics</a></div></div><div class="scroll-cue"><span class="line"></span>Scroll</div></section><section class="page-lead"><div class="wrap page-lead-inner"><p>Clean water is the quiet foundation of almost everything else — a mother washing her hands beside a skilled birth attendant, a girl staying in school without a long walk to a distant borehole, a family surviving the drought cycles that punctuate Garissa’s calendar year. Water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) work is community resilience work.</p></div></section><section class="fn-section" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv fn-head"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The story</span><h2 class="h2">Water that works for <em>everyone.</em></h2></div><p class="fn-intro">Access to clean water protects mothers during pregnancy and delivery, keeps children free of water-borne illness, and spares girls the daily burden that keeps them out of school.</p></div><div class="fn-editorial"><div class="rv fn-art"><img alt="Clean water and community resilience in Garissa" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="60vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fwater.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="rv fn-side"><div class="fn-card"><div class="no">— The story —</div><h3>Why water is health.</h3><p>Clean water is the quiet foundation of health: safer deliveries, healthier children, less illness — and dignity for the women and girls who carry daily water in communities across the county.</p><div class="fn-meta"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l1.9 5.8L20 10l-6.1 1.2L12 17l-1.9-5.8L4 10l6.1-1.2L12 3Z"></path></svg><span><b class="bold">WASH</b> · Water, Sanitation &amp; Hygiene</span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-5.5-7-11a7 7 0 1 1 14 0c0 5.5-7 11-7 11Z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="2.6"></circle></svg><span><b class="bold">Community resilience</b> · natural resources management</span></div></div></div><div class="verify-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"></path></svg><span><b>Note for the team:</b> written from Fountain of Hope’s strategic plan and WASH pillar; confirm the specific site and story with the team for publication.</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="discuss" id="discuss"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv discuss-nav"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The discussion, unpacked</span><h2>Water is <em>resilience.</em></h2><p>In a drought-prone county, a drop of clean water protects the health of everyone it reaches.</p></div><div class="rv discuss-body"><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">01</span> Water, mothers and newborns</h3><p>A safe delivery needs<!-- --> <strong>clean water at every step</strong> — in the home, the health facility and the community. WASH reduces the infections that claim mothers and newborns, and makes every health service safer and more dignified.</p></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">02</span> Water, girls and school</h3><div class="dd-facts"><div class="fact"><div class="k">The daily walk</div><div class="v">Without nearby water, girls carry the burden of collection — a burden that <b>competes with the school day</b>.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">Sanitation &amp; dignity</div><div class="v"><b>Safe facilities and clean water</b> make school a place where girls can manage hygiene and menstruation with dignity.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">Resilience through drought</div><div class="v">Sustainable water access protects households<!-- --> <b>when the rains fail</b> — and protects the gains of every other program.</div></div></div></div><div class="dd-quote"><span class="qmark">“</span><blockquote>Safe water is the foundation of good health — and of a community that can withstand what comes.</blockquote><div class="who">The WASH story · Fountain of Hope, Garissa</div></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">03</span> Real change is built from within</h3><p>Fountain of Hope works with communities, not for them — strengthening local management of water and natural resources so that <strong>the change outlasts any single project</strong>. That is resilience: a community that can meet its own next challenge.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="related" id="related"><div class="wrap"><div class="rel-head rv"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">Keep exploring</span><h2 class="h2">More topics from <em>the field.</em></h2></div></div><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/okoamama-activity-05"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 01</div><h4>When a budget meeting is a life-saving meeting</h4><p>Garissa’s health executive and its budget-makers sit at one table to deliberate maternal and newborn health — and agree the way forward together.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/menstrual-health"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 02</div><h4>Why a girl in Garissa should never miss school because she cannot afford a pad</h4><p>Menstrual health support, dignity kits and school advocacy that keep Garissa’s girls learning.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy)" href="/"><div class="rel-num" style="color:#FF9CBE">All topics</div><h4 style="color:#fff">Back to the Fountain of Hope story</h4><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">Explore the full one-page story and every topic.</p><span class="lnk" style="color:#FF9CBE;margin-top:auto">Open the home page<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="rv cta-in"><span class="eyebrow">Support the work</span><h2>Stand with the women who <em>lead this change.</em></h2><p>Your support funds safe water access and resilience for vulnerable communities in one of Kenya’s most underserved counties.</p><div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="/#footer">Donate now<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#footer">Partner with us</a></div></div></section></main><footer id="footer"><div class="wrap"><div class="foot-grid"><div class="foot-about"><a class="brand" href="/#top"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 